    "https://listings.jobs.gmu.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-tesol-education-tenure-track-tenured-fairfax-va-virginia-united-states-other": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of TESOL Education (Tenure-Track/Tenured)",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of TESOL Education (Tenure-Track/Tenured) - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Assistant or Associate Professor of TESOL Education (Tenure-Track/Tenured) - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor of TESOL Education (Tenure-Track/Tenured) Assistant or Associate Professor of TESOL Education (Tenure-Track/Tenured) 10004674 Fairfax, VA Instructional Faculty Opening on: Oct 20 2026 Department: Col of Ed and Human Development Classification: 9-month Instructional Faculty Job Category: Instructional Faculty Job Type: Full-Time Work Schedule: N/A - I/R Faculty Location: Fairfax, VA Workplace Type: On Site Required Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for visa sponsorship Salary: Salary commensurate with education and experience Criminal Background Check: Yes About the Department: The Department of Teaching and Learning within the College of Education and Human Development (CEHD) offers innovative, transformative, research‑based teacher preparation and educator professional learning pathways. Our nationally recognized programs integrate theory with practical, real-world experience to cultivate reflective, skilled, equity-driven professionals committed to the diverse learners in today’s dynamic educational environments. The Department of Teaching & Learning prepares educators, researchers, and leaders across the P-12 and higher education continuum. Within the Department, the ESOL and World Language Education Program prepares teacher candidates and advanced graduate students to serve multilingual English Learners (ELs) and World Language learners through nationally recognized master’s, certificate, and doctoral coursework. The program sustains critical accreditation, licensure, and school-partnership functions across Northern Virginia—which has the highest concentration of English Learners in the Commonwealth. About the Position: The Tenure-Track/Tenured, Assistant or Associate Professor faculty position will conduct research, teaching, and service within the ESOL and World Language Education Program, with a primary focus in the fields of Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages (TESOL) and multilingual/multicultural education. The position will deliver graduate coursework, mentor doctoral students, pursue externally funded research, and support program accreditation and licensure requirements. This position is essential to sustaining research productivity, instructional capacity, and doctoral student mentorship. Responsibilities: Teaching Teach courses across the ESOL and World Language Education programs (2 courses per fall and spring semester as part of a standard 40/40/20 workload), with emphasis on courses requiring specialized expertise in TESOL, multilingual/multicultural education, and P-12 ESOL licensure-aligned content; and Develop and deliver high-quality online and face-to-face instruction, which includes clinical experiences for teacher candidates. Research Conduct and disseminate original research; Pursue and secure external grant funding, build and lead research teams; Mentor and chair doctoral students’ research, theses, and dissertations; and Maintain an active national/international scholarly profile. Service Provide service to the program, department, college, university, and profession, including supporting accreditation and licensure requirements, contributing to program and curriculum development, engaging in school division and community partnerships, and participating in professional organizations relevant to the field. Required Qualifications: Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in TESOL, applied linguistics, or a closely related field, conferred by the position start date; Established record of externally funded research and scholarly publication; Experience mentoring doctoral students and directing dissertation research; Established record of effective graduate-level teaching, including online instruction; Demonstrated knowledge of TESOL, applied linguistics, and multilingual/multicultural education pedagogy and current research (e.g., translanguaging, multiliteracies, culturally sustaining pedagogy, content-based and disciplinary language instruction, critical language awareness); Exceptional written and verbal communication skills and a collaborative approach to working with colleagues, school division partners, and stakeholders, including multilingual learner families; Demonstrated skill in graduate-level teaching (online, in person, and blended) that engages and inspires a diverse student population; Ability to maintain an active line of research advancing multilingual English learner education, including a record of externally funded projects and publications; Ability to mentor and advise graduate and doctoral students, including guiding dissertation research; and Ability to teach across ESOL and World Language programs, including teacher licensure, master’s, and doctoral-level courses. Preferred Qualifications: Active or eligible P-12 ESOL teaching license preferred; Experience supporting program accreditation and licensure compliance; Experience with online program delivery and recruitment; Experience supervising practicum, field placements, or clinical experiences for teacher candidates; Experience with advocacy for and partnership with multilingual learner communities and families; Prior involvement in professional organizations and a history of fostering collaborative research and school-division partnerships; Record of professional involvement in national and international TESOL, applied linguistics, and/or educational research associations; Specialized expertise in one or more areas of multilingual learner education (e.g., dual language/bilingual education, technology and AI in language education, language assessment, intersection between language and disability, family engagement); Knowledge of accreditation and licensure requirements for teacher preparation programs; Skill in supervising field placements, practicum, and clinical experiences for teacher candidates; Skill in cultivating school division and community partnerships that support program growth and clinical placements; Ability to lead teams, projects, programs, and academic units; and Ability to use of instructional technology and AI effectively for language education. Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applicants must apply for Assistant or Associate Professor of TESOL Education (Tenure-Track/Tenured) at https://jobs.gmu.edu/. Complete and submit the online application to include three professional references with contact information, and provide a Cover Letter/Letter of Intent with CV for review. Posting Open Date: October 20, 2026 For Full Consideration, Apply by: December 8, 2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Mason Ad Statement George Mason University is a nationally ranked R1 research university committed to creating a more just, free, and prosperous world. With 40,000 enrolled students, George Mason is the largest and most diverse public research university in Virginia, offering degree programs at the master's, doctoral, and professional level, along with certificates and credentials. George Mason fosters an All Together Different environment for students, faculty, and staff, driven by our core beliefs. We believe in inclusivity over exclusivity; we believe in advancing our mission by being willing to take risks, not avoiding them; and we believe our best work is possible when we apply our diversity of origin, identity, circumstance, and thought. Equity Statement George Mason University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, committed to promoting inclusion and equity in its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law. Campus Safety Information Mason’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available at http://police.gmu.edu/annual-security-report/ Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1024a28f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Col of Ed and Human Development Col of Ed and Human Development Locations Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 944b3305 Last Name (required) e6807716 Email (required) 7eb840f7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructional Technologist Division of Enrollment Management Join George Mason University as an Instructional Technologist and help advance engaging, innovative online learning through instructional design, educational technology, and faculty support. Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor Antonin Scalia Law School The Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor at George Mason University’s Antonin Scalia Law School has administrative support from various departments within the law school and the university. This position is primarily responsible for supporting student facing office functions including meeting with prospective students, overseeing front desk and staff support, managing office supplies and supporting application management, supporting onboarding functions for admitted students, and guiding current students through their program and university resources. Research Scientist Col of Engineering and Computing The Mason Flood Hazards Research Lab (Sid and Reva Dewberry Department of Civil, Environmental, and Infrastructure Engineering) is seeking a full time Research Scientist. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 9af51533 Last Name (required) 1419bad6 Email (required) 6c344fa1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done N