    "https://listings.jobs.gmu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-research-fellow-mission-systems-engineer-fairfax-va-virginia-united-states-other": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Mission Systems Engineer",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Mission Systems Engineer - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Mission Systems Engineer - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Mission Systems Engineer Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Mission Systems Engineer 10004633 Fairfax, VA Postdoctoral Faculty Opening on: Oct 7 2026 Department: College of Science Classification: Post Doc 12 month Job Category: Postdoctoral Faculty Job Type: Full-Time Work Schedule: Full-time (1.0 FTE, 40 hrs/wk) Location: Fairfax, VA Workplace Type: Hybrid Eligible Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for visa sponsorship Salary: Salary commensurate with education and experience Restricted: Yes Criminal Background Check: Yes About the Department: George Mason University (GMU), a Carnegie Research I institution, is Virginia’s largest and most diverse university with more than 38,000 students. Located in Fairfax, Virginia, Mason is part of the Washington DC metropolitan area offering easy access to the scientific and political resources of the nation’s capital. George Mason University is committed to advancing inclusion, access, and equal opportunity throughout our community. We believe that a broad range of voices, cultures, and perspectives brings vibrancy, innovation, and growth to an academic community. The Landolt Mission team is responsible for developing and executing a NASA space-based mission through coordinated work across science, payload, spacecraft bus, software, systems engineering, integration and test, mission assurance, and project management functions. The unit provides an interdisciplinary research and training environment for faculty, postdoctoral researchers, engineers, staff, and students working collaboratively with federal, academic, commercial, and other external partners. The Landolt Mission team supports mission formulation, systems engineering, subsystem coordination, technical trade studies, requirements development, verification and validation planning, assembly, integration and testing, technical documentation, mission reviews, and mission operations planning. The unit works collaboratively across payload, spacecraft bus, software, ground systems, mission operations, science, and programmatic interfaces to advance mission objectives and meet NASA requirements. Statement on Building an Inclusive Culture: George Mason University College of Science (Mason Science) is committed to advancing inclusive excellence and fostering an environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation throughout our STEM community. At Mason Science, our values include cultivating an organizational culture that promotes belonging, respect, and civility. We believe that varied opinions, cultures, and perspectives are what provides vibrancy, innovation, and growth to an academic community. By prioritizing cultural responsiveness in academics, teaching, research, and global engagement, we strive to attract faculty and staff who exemplify the Mason Science mission and vision. About the Position: This position is sponsored by the NASA Landolt mission. The Postdoctoral Research Mission Systems Engineer (MSE) duties include (at a different level of involvement and responsibility): Contribute to all aspects of mission design, development, and testing by coordinating among subsystem element teams, including payload, software, and hardware teams. Coordinate procedural and regulatory compliance aspects of mission alongside technical aspects. Conceive, conduct, and communicate about necessary trade studies among or within subsystem elements and payload. Organize, oversee, and participate in assembly, integration, and testing of individual components, modules, and satellite bus. As necessary, coordinates and participates in integration of assembled satellite bus with launch vehicle and pad facilities. Identify, support/coordinate, and/or operate relevant simulations and analysis tools to predict, track, and redirect key mission performance parameters, including, but not necessarily limited to, subsystem or overall mass, volume, and power budgets; scientific performance; and risk throughout the system lifecycle. Communicate decision points, outcomes, and summaries upward to all other members of the Landolt Mission team. Document activities for the Landolt Mission through mission reviews, mission reports, mission documentation, technical publications in a manner consistent with space-based projects and published results in professional scientific journals. Work collaboratively and effectively in a team environment composed of scientists, engineers, students, project management and support staff at multiple institutions, federal, academic, and commercial partners. Responsibilities: Execute NASA Landolt Mission throughout its Lifecycle: Lead internal Landolt Mission technical coordination; Work closely with mission leadership and major stakeholders; Co-manage daily operations and resource utilization; and Provide recommendations regarding technical priorities and resource utilization. Mission Systems Development: Conduct and/or oversee trade studies and subsystem analyses; Guide development of Interface Control Documents (ICDs) for all subsystems, including hardware, software, payload, and bus subsystems; Guide, oversee, and participate in all assembly, integration, and test (AI&T) tasks leading to successful integration of payload, bus, software, and complete space vehicle; Identify and comply with all applicable NASA space systems requirements and procedures; and Carry out or oversee system modeling and characterizations of system components and subsystems. Research Support: Conduct mission-relevant research and technical investigations under the guidance of the faculty mentor and Landolt Mission leadership to advance mission science, systems engineering, instrument development, and/or spaceflight technology objectives; Develop, execute, analyze, and document research studies, simulations, models, trade studies, and technical analyses that support Landolt Mission design decisions, performance assessment, risk reduction, and technology maturation; and Review and synthesize relevant scientific, engineering, NASA, and spaceflight literature, standards, and technical documentation to inform mission planning, system development, and research priorities. Reporting: Co-lead the writing and production of formal technical reports, progress reports, and reviews for NASA (e.g., PDR, CDR, TRR, FRR, ORR) in a manner consistent with NASA’s documentation requirements, standards, and guidelines (e.g., NPR 7120.5/8); Write or co-write papers for professional journals and conferences; Attend meetings with sponsors and collaborators, federal, commercial, and academic partners when necessary, occasionally requiring travel outside of the DC metropolitan area; and Assist in the pursuit of new and continued George Mason University Space Center projects and funding support (e.g., new, extended, and follow-on missions/projects). Required Qualifications: Terminal degree in a related field (i.e., PhD or equivalent in Aerospace Engineering or Systems Engineering or related field with an emphasis on space systems development); Experience conducting systems engineering for a relevant project in the space domain or a relevant domain; Knowledge of and ability to conduct systems engineering for a relevant project in the space domain or a relevant domain; Familiarity with systems engineering procedures and practices; and Familiarity with or knowledge of NASA procedures and practices, or with procedures and practices for other spacefaring organizations. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with hybrid missions, operations planning, space hardware, electronics, embedded system development, and NASA procedures and practices; Experience in the design, development, and testing of space instruments, payloads, or electronic systems; Knowledge of and ability to implement or follow NASA procedures and practices; Knowledge of remote sensing missions, technical knowledge of optics, laser systems, space flight hardware, and/or embedded software for space applications are desirable; and Knowledge of hybrid missions and/or operations planning. Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applicants must apply for the Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Mission Systems Engineer at https://jobs.gmu.edu/. Complete and submit the online application to include three professional references with contact information, and provide a CV and a statement of interest and experience. Posting Open Date: October 7, 2026 For Full Consideration, Apply by: November 1, 2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Mason Ad Statement George Mason University is a nationally ranked R1 research university committed to creating a more just, free, and prosperous world. With 40,000 enrolled students, George Mason is the largest and most diverse public research university in Virginia, offering degree programs at the master's, doctoral, and professional level, along with certificates and credentials. George Mason fosters an All Together Different environment for students, faculty, and staff, driven by our core beliefs. We believe in inclusivity over exclusivity; we believe in advancing our mission by being willing to take risks, not avoiding them; and we believe our best work is possible when we apply our diversity of origin, identity, circumstance, and thought. Equity Statement George Mason University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, committed to promoting inclusion and equity in its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law. Campus Safety Information Mason’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available at http://police.gmu.edu/annual-security-report/ Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 150a4801 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Science College of Science Locations Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 76782066 Last Name (required) 288d939d Email (required) ad441047 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructional Technologist Division of Enrollment Management Join George Mason University as an Instructional Technologist and help advance engaging, innovative online learning through instructional design, educational technology, and faculty support. Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor Antonin Scalia Law School The Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor at George Mason University’s Antonin Scalia Law School has administrative support from various departments within the law school and the university. This position is primarily responsible for supporting student facing office functions including meeting with prospective students, overseeing front desk and staff support, managing office supplies and supporting application management, supporting onboarding functions for admitted students, and guiding current students through their program and university resources. Research Scientist Col of Engineering and Computing The Mason Flood Hazards Research Lab (Sid and Reva Dewberry Department of Civil, Environmental, and Infrastructure Engineering) is seeking a full time Research Scientist. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) fffdd17c Last Name (required) e15e1535 Email (required) 20204010 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
