    "https://listings.jobs.gmu.edu/jobs/yu-yuen-kit-yyk-associate-or-full-professor-of-physics-quantum-fairfax-va-virginia-united-states-other": {
      "title": "Yu Yuen Kit (YYK) Associate or Full Professor of Physics - Quantum",
      "description": "Yu Yuen Kit (YYK) Associate or Full Professor of Physics - Quantum - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Yu Yuen Kit (YYK) Associate or Full Professor of Physics - Quantum - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Yu Yuen Kit (YYK) Associate or Full Professor of Physics - Quantum Yu Yuen Kit (YYK) Associate or Full Professor of Physics - Quantum 10004486 Fairfax, VA Instructional Faculty Opening on: Sep 17 2026 Department: College of Science Classification: 9-month Instructional Faculty Job Category: Instructional Faculty Job Type: Full-Time Work Schedule: N/A - I/R Faculty Location: Fairfax, VA Workplace Type: Hybrid Eligible Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for visa sponsorship Salary: Salary commensurate with education and experience Restricted: Yes Criminal Background Check: Yes About the Department: The Department of Physics and Astronomy includes over 40 faculty members, 100 undergraduate students (BS), and 70 graduate students (MS and PhD). Our faculty and students collaborate with local, national, and international research institutions, including the Applied Research Lab, Argonne National Laboratory, CERN, Naval Research Laboratory, National Institute of Standards and Technology, the Institute for Quantum Matter, NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, Space Telescope Science Institute, and the US Naval Observatory. For more information on the department, see http://physics.gmu.edu . George Mason University, a Carnegie Research I institution, is Virginia's largest university with more than 39,000 students representing all 50 states and more than 135 countries. Located in Fairfax, Virginia, Mason is part of the Washington DC metropolitan area offering easy access to the scientific and political resources of the nation's capital. Statement on Building an Inclusive Culture: George Mason University College of Science (Mason Science) is committed to advancing inclusive excellence and fostering an environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation throughout our STEM community. At Mason Science, our values include cultivating an organizational culture that promotes belonging, respect, and civility. We believe that varied opinions, cultures, and perspectives are what provides vibrancy, innovation, and growth to an academic community. By prioritizing cultural responsiveness in academics, teaching, research, and global engagement, we strive to attract faculty and staff who exemplify the Mason Science mission and vision. About the Position: The Yu Yuen Kit (YYK) Associate or Full Professor of Physics in the Department of Physics and Astronomy will be held by an eminent scholar in physics. The first holder of this endowed position will be an expert in theoretical and/or computational quantum science who will relocate their program to George Mason University and collaborate across departments and fields. Responsibilities will include establishing and maintaining an externally funded research group, training graduate students and postdoctoral scholars, teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and collaborating with other George Mason faculty in research and pursuit of center-level funding. The YYK Professor will complement the expertise of existing physics faculty members while also launching new research areas. Responsibilities: Research Develops and maintains an active, externally funded research program; Publishes in high-quality peer-reviewed journals and presents at professional conferences; Supervises research staff, graduate students, and/or postdoctoral fellows; and Contributes to interdisciplinary research initiatives within the department and university. Teaching May teach up to two (2) courses per year or as assigned at the undergraduate and/or graduate level; Advises and mentors students in coursework, research, and professional development; and Contributes to instructional innovation. Service Serves on departmental, college, or university committees as assigned; Participates in professional service (e.g., reviewing for journals, serving on grant panels); and Contributes to outreach, engagement, and initiatives that support the mission of the university. Required Qualifications: Terminal degree/PhD in Physics or a related field; Experience in quantum physics which includes, but is not limited to, quantum information science, quantum devices, quantum materials, and quantum sensing; Rank of Associate Professor (or equivalent) or higher; Success in securing external research funding; Strong record of scholarly production; Knowledge of theoretical and/or computational quantum science at a depth demonstrated by a sustained, internationally recognized record of peer-reviewed scholarship; Knowledge of the physics curriculum sufficient to teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels; Knowledge of federal and non-federal research funding mechanisms, including center-level and multi-investigator programs; Skill in preparing competitive research proposals to federal agencies and other external sponsors; Skill in mentoring and supervising graduate students and postdoctoral scholars; Skill in scientific writing, oral presentation, and classroom instruction; Ability to establish and maintain an externally funded research group; Ability to collaborate across departments and disciplines, including in the pursuit of center-level funding; Ability to launch new research directions that complement existing departmental expertise; A record of research, teaching, and service supporting appointment at the rank of associate professor or professor with tenure; and Standing as an eminent scholar in physics evidenced by honors, fellowships, editorial or advisory roles, or comparable external recognition. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated excellence in teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applicants must apply for Yu Yuen Kit (YYK) Associate or Full Professor of Physics - Quantum at https://jobs.gmu.edu/. Complete and submit the online application to include three professional references with contact information, and provide a Cover Letter/Letter of Intent, CV, Research Statement, Teaching Statement and please provide the names, affiliations, and emails of 3 individuals who can write a letter of recommendation. Posting Open Date: September 17, 2026 For Full Consideration, Apply by: November 15, 2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Mason Ad Statement George Mason University is a nationally ranked R1 research university committed to creating a more just, free, and prosperous world. With 40,000 enrolled students, George Mason is the largest and most diverse public research university in Virginia, offering degree programs at the master's, doctoral, and professional level, along with certificates and credentials. George Mason fosters an All Together Different environment for students, faculty, and staff, driven by our core beliefs. We believe in inclusivity over exclusivity; we believe in advancing our mission by being willing to take risks, not avoiding them; and we believe our best work is possible when we apply our diversity of origin, identity, circumstance, and thought. Equity Statement George Mason University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, committed to promoting inclusion and equity in its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law. Campus Safety Information Mason’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available at http://police.gmu.edu/annual-security-report/ Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ad9f59e1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Science College of Science Locations Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 76bd9e05 Last Name (required) 880f4f94 Email (required) 1f203694 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructional Technologist Division of Enrollment Management Join George Mason University as an Instructional Technologist and help advance engaging, innovative online learning through instructional design, educational technology, and faculty support. Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor Antonin Scalia Law School The Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor at George Mason University’s Antonin Scalia Law School has administrative support from various departments within the law school and the university. This position is primarily responsible for supporting student facing office functions including meeting with prospective students, overseeing front desk and staff support, managing office supplies and supporting application management, supporting onboarding functions for admitted students, and guiding current students through their program and university resources. Research Scientist Col of Engineering and Computing The Mason Flood Hazards Research Lab (Sid and Reva Dewberry Department of Civil, Environmental, and Infrastructure Engineering) is seeking a full time Research Scientist. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) d748f61e Last Name (required) a61d7de5 Email (required) e587fa2f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right