    "https://listings.jobs.gmu.edu/jobs/term-instructional-professor-and-law-library-director-arlington-va-virginia-united-states-other": {
      "title": "Term Instructional Professor and Law Library Director",
      "description": "Term Instructional Professor and Law Library Director - Arlington, VA, Virginia, United States Term Instructional Professor and Law Library Director - Arlington, VA, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Term Instructional Professor and Law Library Director Term Instructional Professor and Law Library Director 10004522 Arlington, VA Instructional Faculty Opening on: Sep 15 2026 Department: Antonin Scalia Law School Classification: 12-month Instructional Faculty Job Category: Instructional Faculty Job Type: Full-Time Work Schedule: Full time (1.0 FTE, 40 hrs/wk) Location: Arlington, VA Workplace Type: On Site Required Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for visa sponsorship Salary: Salary commensurate with education and experience Criminal Background Check: Yes About the Department: The Antonin Scalia Law School strives to be a national leader in legal education; applying tools of economics and other social sciences to the study of legal doctrine, process, and institutions. The Law School prepares students to practice law in a broad range of public and private sector organizations within the Commonwealth and around the country. In addition, it produces academic scholarship that expands society's understanding of law and legal institutions with a special focus on using economic tools and methods to do so. About the Position: The primary purpose of law faculty is to provide effective teaching to Juris Doctor students, produce original scholarly works for publication, and provide service, including leadership, through participation in governance, and operational or development activities in the Law School, the university, and/or the legal profession. Additionally, in accordance with ABA law school accreditation standards, law faculty share with the dean the primary responsibility and authority for planning, implementing, and administering the program of legal education; selection, retention, promotion and tenure of faculty; and determining educational policy. Term Instructional Professor Responsibilities: Teaching Designs course curricula, prepares for classes, is available for consultation about those classes, assesses student performance in those classes, and remains current in subjects being taught in accordance with ABA standards. Effective teaching requires a combination of course and curricular materials, developed learning outcomes, and thoughtful assignments and assessments designed to promote student learning. Service Engages in service to the Law School and university community, participates in governance of the law school as requested/allowed, curricular development, and other institutional responsibilities as required by ABA accreditation standards; Provides service to the profession, works with judges and practicing lawyers to improve the profession; and Provides service to the public including participation in pro bono activities. Examples include, but are not limited to, attendance at faculty meetings; curricular development; support for co-curricular student experiences; committee participation; leadership in professional organizations. Law Library Director Responsibilities: Provides strategic leadership for the law library's instructional and research support programs; Teaches assigned law school courses or is embedded within other courses, including legal research in LRWA I, II, III, and IV, Scholarly Writing, and advanced legal research courses, and other applicable courses within the instructor’s area(s) of interest and expertise; teaches workshops and other pedagogical sessions offered by the Library; Collaborates with faculty to integrate research skills and information literacy competencies throughout the law school curriculum; Oversees the development of the library’s instructional services and materials to faculty, students, staff, alumni, and the local bar; Coordinates law school efforts training students in the effective use of legal databases, artificial intelligence tools, and emerging technologies relevant to legal practice; Provides research consultations to support student academic work; Supervises and mentors law librarians and other instructional personnel engaged in teaching activities; May support the work of a Library RA(s); Participates in faculty governance through attendance and participation in faculty meetings and service on standing law school and/or university committees, including as a voting member on the law school’s Library Faculty and Technology Committee; Prepares for and attends faculty meetings as a limited voting member; Serves on law school and/or university committees, as assigned; Provides library and research updates to the full faculty, as needed; Participates in law school events in support of students, prospective students, faculty, and alumni engagement; Provides strategic leadership for the law library in support of the law school's mission and goals; Ensures compliance with applicable ABA standards relating to library resources and services; Directs all operations of the law library, including services, collections, facilities, technology, and personnel; Develops and manages the Library & Technology budget to: Direct the growth and development of the collection, physical plant, and equipment to support the instructional, research, and service missions of the law school; Provides personnel and services to support the instructional, research, and service missions of the law school; Supports faculty research, scholarship, and publication efforts; Works with Head of Technical Services and Collections Development to Negotiate contracts and licenses with publishers, database vendors, and service providers; Evaluates and implement emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence and legal analytics tools; Sets and communicates library policies and procedures to all stakeholders; Establishes performance expectations and professional development opportunities for library employees; Manages staffing levels and organizational structure to meet evolving institutional needs; Assists in managing the law school’s listservs and generic email accounts; Represents the library on matters related to Library & Technology within the law school and university, and to external consortia and professional organizations; Participates in professional development and contributes to the law librarian profession; and Other duties related to the position as assigned that help the department achieve its objectives and goals and/or support the mission of the Law School as determined by the employee's supervisor. Required Qualifications: JD and MLS required; Experience conducting legal research and writing; Substantial experience in a law library or similar setting; Supervisory experience; Legal knowledge in substantive legal field(s), which must at least include legal research; Highly knowledgeable in computer applications and technologies employed in law schools today; and Areas of expertise must include instruction on legal research and technology; Preferred Qualifications: Experience with law-school related technology; Experience using AI research tools in a legal setting; Demonstrated teaching ability; and Familiarity with AI research tools. Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applicants must apply for Term Instructional Professor and Law Library Director at https://jobs.gmu.edu/. Complete and submit the online application to include three professional references with contact information, and provide a cover letter and CV for review. Posting Open Date: September 15, 2026 For Full Consideration, Apply by: October 31, 2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Mason Ad Statement George Mason University is a nationally ranked R1 research university committed to creating a more just, free, and prosperous world. With 40,000 enrolled students, George Mason is the largest and most diverse public research university in Virginia, offering degree programs at the master's, doctoral, and professional level, along with certificates and credentials. George Mason fosters an All Together Different environment for students, faculty, and staff, driven by our core beliefs. We believe in inclusivity over exclusivity; we believe in advancing our mission by being willing to take risks, not avoiding them; and we believe our best work is possible when we apply our diversity of origin, identity, circumstance, and thought. Equity Statement George Mason University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, committed to promoting inclusion and equity in its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law. Campus Safety Information Mason’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available at http://police.gmu.edu/annual-security-report/ Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c7b3c23a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Antonin Scalia Law School Antonin Scalia Law School Locations Arlington, VA, Virginia, United States Arlington, VA, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 8f63499a Last Name (required) 088138ab Email (required) a035ec08 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructional Technologist Division of Enrollment Management Join George Mason University as an Instructional Technologist and help advance engaging, innovative online learning through instructional design, educational technology, and faculty support. Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor Antonin Scalia Law School The Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor at George Mason University’s Antonin Scalia Law School has administrative support from