    "https://listings.jobs.gmu.edu/jobs/school-of-nursing-assistant-associate-professor-fairfax-va-virginia-united-states-other": {
      "title": "School of Nursing - Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "School of Nursing - Assistant/Associate Professor - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States School of Nursing - Assistant/Associate Professor - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode School of Nursing - Assistant/Associate Professor School of Nursing - Assistant/Associate Professor 10004291 Fairfax, VA Instructional Faculty Opening on: Sep 3 2026 Department: College of Public Health Classification: 9-month Instructional Faculty Job Category: Instructional Faculty Job Type: Full-Time Work Schedule: Full-time (1.0 FTE, 40 hrs/wk) Location: Fairfax, VA Workplace Type: On Site Required Sponsorship Eligibility: Eligible for visa sponsorship Salary: Salary commensurate with education and experience Criminal Background Check: Yes Works with Minors check: Yes About the Department: For over 50 years, the School of Nursing has prepared students for interdisciplinary roles as clinicians, educators, researchers, and administrators. Students learn to address the challenges of a rapidly changing and diverse healthcare environment with hands-on experience in simulation, skill-building labs, and clinical settings. Within the school’s Mason and Partner Clinics (https://publichealth.gmu.edu/mapclinics), they gain experience working with culturally diverse patient populations in the Northern Virginia area which provides them with the necessary skills to deliver health care where it's needed the most. Nursing faculty, staff, and students engage in work, study, and research that have major impacts on health equity, vulnerable populations, preventative care, population health, and the local workforce. Serving as experts in workforce development, School of Nursing faculty are committed to challenging the national nursing shortage and producing talented, equity-minded practitioners and scholars. About the Position: Faculty contribute to the mission of the School of Nursing through innovative and impactful education, research, and service. The School of Nursing - Assistant/Associate Professor serves as teaching-intensive faculty across nursing school curricula, depending upon the area of their expertise and the needs of the school. Priority consideration is given to individuals with a background or experience in Med/Surg, Critical Care, or Maternal/Child Health. Responsibilities: Teaches clinical and non-clinical courses across School of Nursing curriculum, consistent with general and/or specialized nursing background/expertise. Engages in professional and academic service that advances the priority goals of the program, School of Nursing, College of Public Health, and participates in faculty governance. Required Qualifications: Terminal degree in Nursing (DNP or PhD) or health-related field; At least 3 years of clinical expertise as a medical-surgical nurse, pediatrics, and/or maternal/child nurse; An unencumbered Virginia Registered Nurse and Nurse Practitioner License, or eligibility to obtain upon employment; Knowledge of: Advanced Nursing Practice: Deep understanding of nursing theories, principles, and practices. This includes specialized knowledge in a specialty area of nursing practice and understanding of current healthcare laws, policies, ethics, and economics as they affect patient care and the nursing profession. Must have the knowledge and skills to teach didactic and/or clinical courses related to med/surg, critical care, or maternal/child health. Research Methods: Knowledge of evidence-based practice and research methodologies pertinent to the nursing field. Education Techniques: Familiarity with curriculum development, pedagogical theories, and teaching strategies specific to higher education and nursing education. Skills in: Communication: Excellent verbal and written communication skills for interacting with students, colleagues, and the wider academic and healthcare community. Leadership and Collaboration: Capacity to lead projects and work collaboratively with other faculty members, as well as participate in committees and contribute to the academic community. Demonstrated organizational skills. Abilities in: Teaching: Ability to effectively impart knowledge, facilitate learning, and assess student performance in a variety of course formats (traditional, hybrid, and distance education). This includes lecturing, course design using learning management systems, demonstrating practical applications related to course content, and mentoring students. Adaptability: Ability to adapt teaching methods to different learning styles and environments, including online platforms. Critical Thinking: Capability to engage in reflective and analytical thinking, crucial for both teaching and research. Problem Solving: Ability to address academic and administrative problems that may arise in managing research, courses, and programs within the school. Mentoring: Aptitude for guiding students and junior faculty members, as appropriate per rank, in their academic and professional development. Collaboration and Collegiality: Ability to work in a team-based environment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching in higher education. Experience with curriculum design, program evaluation, and accreditation processes. Experience with evidence-based pedagogy. Record of scholarly productivity (publications, presentations, or funded projects). Active participation in professional organizations related to advanced practice nursing. Knowledge of: Accreditation: Familiarity with accreditation standards for Nursing programs. Abilities in: Clinical Teaching/Supervision: Ability to teach or supervise students in clinical coursework in med/surg, critical care, or maternal/child health. Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applicants must apply for the School of Nursing - Assistant/Associate Professor (Requisition #10004291) at https://jobs.gmu.edu/. Complete and submit the online application to include three professional references with contact information (one of which must be a current or past supervisor), and provide 1) cover letter/letter of intent, 2) CV, and 3) brief teaching philosophy statement. Posting Open Date: September 3, 2026 For Full Consideration, Apply by: September 16, 2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Mason Ad Statement George Mason University is a nationally ranked R1 research university committed to creating a more just, free, and prosperous world. With 40,000 enrolled students, George Mason is the largest and most diverse public research university in Virginia, offering degree programs at the master's, doctoral, and professional level, along with certificates and credentials. George Mason fosters an All Together Different environment for students, faculty, and staff, driven by our core beliefs. We believe in inclusivity over exclusivity; we believe in advancing our mission by being willing to take risks, not avoiding them; and we believe our best work is possible when we apply our diversity of origin, identity, circumstance, and thought. Equity Statement George Mason University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, committed to promoting inclusion and equity in its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law. Campus Safety Information Mason’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available at http://police.gmu.edu/annual-security-report/ Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 9fb9b588 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Public Health College of Public Health Locations Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 280cfefb Last Name (required) 79321c04 Email (required) 7c65a142 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructional Technologist Division of Enrollment Management Join George Mason University as an Instructional Technologist and help advance engaging, innovative online learning through instructional design, educational technology, and faculty support. Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor Antonin Scalia Law School The Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor at George Mason University’s Antonin Scalia Law School has administrative support from various departments within the law school and the university. This position is primarily responsible for supporting student facing office functions including meeting with prospective students, overseeing front desk and staff support, managing office supplies and supporting application management, supporting onboarding functions for admitted students, and guiding current students through their program and university resources. Research Scientist Col of Engineering and Computing The Mason Flood Hazards Research Lab (Sid and Reva Dewberry Department of Civil, Environmental, and Infrastructure Engineering) is seeking a full time Research Scientist. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) ccb07628 Last Name (required) 8f422d7b Email (required) a0d89c3f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
