    "https://listings.jobs.gmu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-fairfax-va-virginia-united-states-other-0fb34bb5-e349-4c26-b4d1-6ceee8459571": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor - Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor Assistant Professor 10004318 Fairfax, VA Instructional Faculty Opening on: Jul 30 2026 Department: Costello College of Business Classification: 9-month Instructional Faculty Job Category: Instructional Faculty Job Type: Full-Time Work Schedule: Full-time (1.0 FTE, 40 hrs/wk) Location: Fairfax, VA Workplace Type: On Site Required Sponsorship Eligibility: Eligible for visa sponsorship Salary: Salary commensurate with education and experience Criminal Background Check: Yes About the Department: The Donald G. Costello College of Business at George Mason University is one of the largest business schools in Virginia. While its main campus is located near Washington, D.C. in Fairfax, Virginia, Mason also has campuses in Arlington, VA and Incheon, South Korea. The college’s AACSB-accredited business and accounting curricula prepare undergraduate and graduate students from the U.S. and across the globe for career success in business and government. Its research-based faculty focus on multi-disciplinary academic programs, inclusive entrepreneurship, modular education, experiential learning, and corporate partner engagement. Through such efforts, Mason is transforming the landscape of business education and workforce development. Learn more at business.gmu.edu. Management is one of six areas within the Costello College of Business. With 11 tenure-line faculty and 5 term faculty, the Management Area has faculty with expertise in many different business topics spanning from entrepreneurship to strategy to organizational behavior. Faculty have published their work in top management journals including Administrative Science Quarterly, Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Journal, Journal of Business Venturing, Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice, and more. The Area offers courses in relevant topics (e.g., the College’s capstone strategy course) as well as minors in entrepreneurship and international business. About the Position: The Management Area seeks candidates for two tenure-line positions in Strategy and/or Entrepreneurship. As the Costello College of Business, we value faculty whose scholarship represents a consistent pipeline of research that: Addresses significant problems affecting business and society; such research should have the potential for meaningful impact in terms of organizational design, firm and regulatory policy, and/or the behaviors of economic agents (e.g., consumers, employees); demonstrates the highest levels of methodological rigor, leveraging innovative qualitative and quantitative methods to analyze generalizable data representing real-world contexts and problems; is targeted for, and published in, the highest quality journals; consists of clear theoretical, contextual, or methodological themes that demonstrate the identity of the faculty member as a thought leader in their field; and showcases the unique contributions of that faculty member. For these positions we welcome applicants whose research addresses important problems affecting business and society through a focus on strategic management, entrepreneurship, innovation, venture creation and growth, entrepreneurial strategy, technology commercialization, strategic renewal, corporate entrepreneurship, ecosystems, global strategy, economics, and other areas related to strategy. Candidates should also demonstrate an established record of teaching effectiveness, including a commitment to course design, supporting and engaging students, and continued faculty growth as regards pedagogy. Candidates should be able to contribute to courses in strategy and/or entrepreneurship, including the College’s capstone strategy course, entrepreneurship offerings, innovation-related courses, and/or doctoral seminars. There is also significant leeway for candidates to develop their own classes and contribute to the offerings of the area. Candidates should have consistent and clear evidence of collegiality and collaboration and be willing to contribute to various areas of service at Costello. Responsibilities: Conducts impactful research for publication in top-tier academic journals; Teaches Management area courses in undergraduate and/or graduate programs; Provides service to the Management Area, the Costello College of Business, the University, and the profession; and Be invested as a team member in helping colleagues and the College further our collective goals. Required Qualifications: Terminal degree in a related field; PhD or equivalent, or be ABD with a documented expectation of degree completion before the start of Fall 2027; Evidence of potential to teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels; and An impactful research stream that changes the way we view important problems facing business and society. Preferred Qualifications: Assistant Professors with three or more years of experience; History of working with PhD students; and Interest in exploring the use of modern technology (e.g., AI) in teaching and/or research. Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applicants must apply for the Assistant Professor at https://jobs.gmu.edu/. Complete and submit the online application to include three professional references with contact information, and provide a letter of intent, CV, research statement, and teaching statement. Posting Open Date: July 30, 2026 For Full Consideration, Apply by: September 1, 2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Mason Ad Statement George Mason University is a nationally ranked R1 research university committed to creating a more just, free, and prosperous world. With 40,000 enrolled students, George Mason is the largest and most diverse public research university in Virginia, offering degree programs at the master's, doctoral, and professional level, along with certificates and credentials. George Mason fosters an All Together Different environment for students, faculty, and staff, driven by our core beliefs. We believe in inclusivity over exclusivity; we believe in advancing our mission by being willing to take risks, not avoiding them; and we believe our best work is possible when we apply our diversity of origin, identity, circumstance, and thought. Equity Statement George Mason University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, committed to promoting inclusion and equity in its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law. Campus Safety Information Mason’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available at http://police.gmu.edu/annual-security-report/ Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 4f40274d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Costello College of Business Costello College of Business Locations Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States Fairfax, VA, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 813221c5 Last Name (required) c4af8ace Email (required) e85db535 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructional Technologist Division of Enrollment Management Join George Mason University as an Instructional Technologist and help advance engaging, innovative online learning through instructional design, educational technology, and faculty support. Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor Antonin Scalia Law School The Graduate Admissions Specialist & Academic Advisor at George Mason University’s Antonin Scalia Law School has administrative support from various departments within the law school and the university. This position is primarily responsible for supporting student facing office functions including meeting with prospective students, overseeing front desk and staff support, managing office supplies and supporting application management, supporting onboarding functions for admitted students, and guiding current students through their program and university resources. Research Scientist Col of Engineering and Computing The Mason Flood Hazards Research Lab (Sid and Reva Dewberry Department of Civil, Environmental, and Infrastructure Engineering) is seeking a full time Research Scientist. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 7c85134a Last Name (required) 7543c17a Email (required) 64f6e863 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
